httpjet (0.2.2-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * HTTP/3: keep the handshake slot of a connection lost before its handshake
    when a second datagram has it serviced again before the reap; pairs of
    spoofed Initials no longer stay under the Retry threshold.
  * Rewrite: re-parse an access file whose ctime, size or inode changed, not
    only its mtime (a reload kept the old rules after cp -p or rsync -t);
    key a cached rewrite outcome by the rule sets that produced it.
  * subFilter: ask a proxied upstream for the identity entity so its body is
    filtered; leave a backend HEAD without a length instead of 0; do not
    advertise byte ranges under a filtered context.
  * ACME: drop a refused or failed order instead of retrying it forever; cap
    Retry-After at seven days; vary the renewal jitter between accounts.
  * Page cache: a shared-path parameter must carry a value; a tag purge of an
    entry that never reached the file tier keeps the boot scan from restoring
    an older version; the admission filter takes one counter per quarter of
    its block (less than half the false positives).
  * FastCGI: wake one waiting caller per freed pool slot. Basic auth: count
    an IPv6 /64 as one client.
  * HTTP/2: find the Link early-hint anchor with memchr. HTTP/1: name
    truncated requests and body timeouts among the connection-end causes.

 -- Mike Fara <35661811+faratech@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000

httpjet (0.2.1-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Page cache: size the store-admission filter so a never-requested URL
    reads zero; --page-cache-admit-threshold 2 had decayed into storing every
    cacheable response. Reject a boot-scan install of a file a tag purge
    swept; count fan-out directories the boot scan cannot read.
  * Hardening: keep the LSAPI length-prefix guards in release builds; map the
    lsphp generation file raw; refuse OpenSSL majors the OCSP prototypes were
    not compared with.
  * Count HTTP/1 connection ends by cause; expose the admission table's size
    and occupancy.
  * HTTP/2: reuse flush metadata and coalesce adjacent inline frames; count
    in-flight requests on per-worker cache lines.
  * Tests: fuzz targets for HTTP/2 frames, the HTTP/3 wire parsers, LSAPI
    packets, FastCGI records and the page-cache container.

 -- Mike Fara <35661811+faratech@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000

httpjet (0.2.0-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Security: validate the upstream WebSocket handshake; strip credentials and
    keep non-ASCII cookie lines in capsule revalidation; decode every gzip
    member of a backend response; fail an LSAPI response whose stream packet
    precedes its header; escape control characters in the text error log;
    refuse an LSAPI socket path another live process serves.
  * QUIC: drop connections lost before their handshake and keep their slot
    counted; send Drained exactly once; charge shared cache bodies to the
    connection only.
  * Startup: build the rewrite prefilter off the request path, parse each
    .htaccess once and before serving, and reuse parsed files across reloads.
  * Steer listeners by CPU only when the NIC's receive fan-out reaches every
    worker; count HTTP/2 connection ends and page-cache ghost hits.
  * Packaging: fix the lsphp reload unit, readiness-marker reads, TLS pair
    validation and the installer tests.

 -- Mike Fara <35661811+faratech@users.noreply.github.com>  Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000

httpjet (0.1.12-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Reduce hot-path allocation and contention: borrowed vhost routing,
    a single-pass fast-serve header scan, HPACK header-name reuse, and
    sharded telemetry and bridge counters.
  * Refine the page-cache disk store and metadata blob handling, the
    fast-memo and page-memo serve paths, and access-log rendering.

 -- Mike Fara <35661811+faratech@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 08 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000

httpjet (0.1.11-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Default the io_uring transport to cooperative task running
    (--uring-ring coop) and enable the page-cache response memo for cookieless
    public hits (--no-page-cache-response-memo disables it).
  * Steer accepted connections to the CPU that received them (SO_INCOMING_CPU;
    --no-cpu-steering disables it), reuse HTTP/1.1 write buffers, reuse the
    encoded HPACK Date literal and format access-log lines without core::fmt.
  * Schedule HTTP/3 streams fairly and add opt-in HTTP/3 send experiments:
    --h3-engine, --h3-send-batch and --h3-gso-segments.

